      "measured": true,
      "title": "El coraz\u00f3n del movimiento",
      "year": 2025,
      "medium": "Oil on canvas",
      "description": "In the Mexica worldview, to possess a heart (Yollotl) is to be in a state of constant movement (Ollin). There is an ancient vibration in the teyolia-the vital life force of consciousness. This narrative traces back to the very origin of Mexico City: the heart of the warrior Copil cast into the waters of Lake Texcoco, germinating into a sacred nopal cactus where an eagle descended to mark the center of the world.",
