      "year": 2025,
      "medium": "Oil on canvas",
      "description": "In this painting, I sought to bridge the physical intensity of an Arctic seal hunt with the metaphysical presence of Sila, the spirit of the air and life force. Inspired by a journey to Iqaluit and the stories shared by a close friend, the work captures the surreal brilliance of a day moon over the polynia (the water that never freezes). The stark contrast between the deep blue water and the vibrant red of seal blood on the ice serves as a grounding point for the ethereal spirals that dance through the composition. These spirals are not just shapes; they are Sila herself, weaving together my friend's life journey, the memory of our shared expedition, and the enduring, breathing energy that animates the frozen landscape.",
